-- Issues found while encoding are numbered in ISSUES.md; a comment "ISSUE n"
-- below points to the entry.

IMPORT support

§ `Part 1 — Preliminary`

§§ `Division 1 — Preliminary (ss 1–5)`

-- s 1  Short title: the Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Act 2026.
-- s 3  Simplified outline: not operative (Legislation Act / drafting
--      convention). It is NOT encoded, and it does not match the operative
--      text in one respect: ISSUE 1.
-- s 4  Application within and outside Australia, every external Territory.
-- s 5  Binds the Crown in right of the Commonwealth, not of a State, the ACT
--      or the NT.
-- None of ss 1, 3, 4, 5 decides a case the rest of this encoding asks about.

-- s 2  Commencement: the whole Act, the day after Royal Assent.
@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 2(1), table item 1
GIVEN `the day of Royal Assent` IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`s 2 — the day this Act commences, given` `the day of Royal Assent` MEANS
    `the date` y m (d + 1)
    WHERE
        y MEANS IF lastDayOfYear THEN `the day of Royal Assent`'s `year` + 1 ELSE `the day of Royal Assent`'s `year`
        m MEANS BRANCH
                    IF lastDayOfYear THEN 1
                    IF lastDayOfMonth THEN `the day of Royal Assent`'s `month` + 1
                    OTHERWISE `the day of Royal Assent`'s `month`
        d MEANS IF lastDayOfMonth THEN 0 ELSE `the day of Royal Assent`'s `day`
        lastDayOfMonth MEANS
            `the day of Royal Assent`'s `day` EQUALS
                `the number of days in month` (`the day of Royal Assent`'s `month`) `of year` (`the day of Royal Assent`'s `year`)
        lastDayOfYear MEANS lastDayOfMonth AND `the day of Royal Assent`'s `month` EQUALS 12

§§ `Division 2 — Definitions and key concepts`

§§§ `s 7 — What is a designated diplomatic office?`

-- The offices of the Commonwealth the Bill names, plus the office
-- prescribed by the rules under s 7(2). An office not on the list and not
-- prescribed is not designated, and the Act says nothing about it.
DECLARE `Office of the Commonwealth` IS ONE OF
    `Ambassador to the United States of America`                                                     -- (a)
    `Consul-General in the United States of America` HAS `the post` IS A STRING                      -- (b) "any office of"
    `High Commissioner to the United Kingdom`                                                        -- (c)
    `High Commissioner to New Zealand`                                                               -- (d)
    `Ambassador to Ireland`                                                                          -- (e)
    `Ambassador to the Netherlands`                                                                  -- (f)
    `High Commissioner to India`                                                                     -- (g)
    `Ambassador to the Holy See`                                                                     -- (h)
    `High Commissioner to Singapore`                                                                 -- (i)
    `Ambassador to Japan`                                                                            -- (j)
    `Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the OECD`                                            -- (k)
    `Ambassador to Italy`                                                                            -- (l)
    `High Commissioner to Canada`                                                                    -- (m)
    `Ambassador to Belgium`                                                                          -- (n)
    `Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the United Nations` HAS `the post` IS A STRING       -- (o) "any office of"
    `another office of the Commonwealth` HAS
        `the name of the office`                         IS A STRING
        `in a country or place outside Australia`        IS A BOOLEAN
        `prescribed by the rules`                        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 7
GIVEN `the office` IS AN `Office of the Commonwealth`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` `the office` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `another office of the Commonwealth` n outside prescribed THEN
        "(2) an office ... outside Australia ... prescribed by the rules" ... outside AND prescribed
    OTHERWISE
        "(1)(a)-(o) one of the listed offices" ... TRUE

§§§ `s 8 — Political affiliations relevant to diplomatic appointments`

-- The legislatures named in s 8(1) and s 8(2)(a).
DECLARE `Legislature` IS ONE OF
    `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`
    `the Parliament of a State`
    `the legislature of a Territory`

-- A period of membership. `ended` is NOTHING while the person is still a
-- member. When membership begins (election, declaration of the poll, start of
-- term, swearing-in) is the caller's question: ISSUE 9.
DECLARE `Period of membership` HAS
    `legislature` IS A `Legislature`
    `began`       IS A `Calendar date`
    `ended`       IS A MAYBE `Calendar date`

-- s 8(2)(b)(i)-(vi): positions whose staff count. `some other position`
-- (a backbench member or senator, a Presiding Officer, a whip, ...) is the
-- off-list case and is deliberately not a disjunct below.
-- (b)(i) uses "Minister" in its ordinary sense, not the s 6 defined sense:
-- ISSUE 6.
DECLARE `Position of a parliamentarian` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister (including the Prime Minister)`
    `the Leader of the Opposition in the Senate`
    `the Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives`
    `the Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the Senate`
    `the Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives`
    `a shadow Minister`
    `some other position`

-- s 8(2)(b): one engagement under the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984.
-- `the position occupied by the employer` is the position the employing
-- parliamentarian held during the engagement. Whether an electorate officer of
-- a Minister counts is open: ISSUE 7.
DECLARE `Engagement under the MOP(S) Act` HAS
    `the position occupied by the employer` IS A `Position of a parliamentarian`

-- s 8(2)(c): one engagement as staff of a State or Territory office-holder.
-- Both limbs are open-textured and are the caller's answer: ISSUE 8.
DECLARE `Engagement as State or Territory political staff` HAS
    `employed under a law of a State or Territory`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer's position is equivalent or corresponds to one in (b)(i) to (vi)`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 8(2)(d): one role with a political party. Whether the party must have
-- been registered at the time of the role, or now: ISSUE 10.
DECLARE `Capacity in a party` IS ONE OF
    `an officer`
    `an employee`
    `a member only`

DECLARE `Role with a political party` HAS
    `capacity`                                                              IS A `Capacity in a party`
    `the party is registered under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918`     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Person` HAS
    `name`                                          IS A STRING
    `periods of membership of a legislature`        IS A LIST OF `Period of membership`
    `engagements under the MOP(S) Act`              IS A LIST OF `Engagement under the MOP(S) Act`
    `engagements as State or Territory political staff` IS A LIST OF `Engagement as State or Territory political staff`
    `roles with political parties`                  IS A LIST OF `Role with a political party`

-- "the last 10 years" has no stated reference point. The encoding measures
-- it back from the day of the step being tested (the list, the appointment,
-- the acting arrangement), and includes the first day of the window: ISSUE 4.
GIVEN `the day` IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`the first day of the last 10 years before` `the day` MEANS
    `the day` `minus calendar years` 10

-- A membership period that had begun by the day and had not ended before the
-- window opened.
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Period of membership`
      `the day`    IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the period` `falls at any time within the last 10 years before` `the day` MEANS
        (`the period`'s `began` `is on or before` `the day`)
    AND CONSIDER `the period`'s `ended`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST e  THEN (`the first day of the last 10 years before` `the day`) `is on or before` e

-- A membership period some part of which lies before the window opened.
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Period of membership`
      `the day`    IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the period` `falls at a time other than within the last 10 years before` `the day` MEANS
    `the period`'s `began` `is before` (`the first day of the last 10 years before` `the day`)

@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 8(1)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person`
      `the day`    IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `the person` `on` `the day` MEANS
    "is, or has been at any time within the last 10 years, a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth, the Parliament of a State or the legislature of a Territory"
    ... `at least one of` (`the person`'s `periods of membership of a legislature`) `satisfies` inWindow
    WHERE
        inWindow p MEANS p `falls at any time within the last 10 years before` `the day`

@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 8(2)(b)(i)-(vi)
GIVEN `the position` IS A `Position of a parliamentarian`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a position listed in s 8(2)(b)` `the position` MEANS
    NOT `the position` EQUALS `some other position`

@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 8(2)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person`
      `the day`    IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `the person` `on` `the day` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `at least one of` (`the person`'s `periods of membership of a legislature`) `satisfies` beforeWindow
    ..  "(b)" ... `at least one of` (`the person`'s `engagements under the MOP(S) Act`) `satisfies` listedEmployer
    ..  "(c)" ... `at least one of` (`the person`'s `engagements as State or Territory political staff`) `satisfies` correspondingEmployer
    OR  "(d)" ... `at least one of` (`the person`'s `roles with political parties`) `satisfies` officerOrEmployee
    WHERE
        beforeWindow p MEANS
            p `falls at a time other than within the last 10 years before` `the day`
        listedEmployer e MEANS
            `is a position listed in s 8(2)(b)` (e's `the position occupied by the employer`)
        correspondingEmployer e MEANS
                e's `employed under a law of a State or Territory`
            AND e's `the employer's position is equivalent or corresponds to one in (b)(i) to (vi)`
        officerOrEmployee r MEANS
                r's `the party is registered under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918`
            AND NOT r's `capacity` EQUALS `a member only`

-- The two affiliations together, as s 11(2) and s 9(1)/(3) use them.
DECLARE `Political affiliation` IS ONE OF
    `a disqualifying political affiliation`
    `a significant political affiliation (and no disqualifying one)`
    `neither`

GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person`
      `the day`    IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Political affiliation`
`the political affiliation of` `the person` `on` `the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `the person` `on` `the day`
            THEN `a disqualifying political affiliation`
        IF `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `the person` `on` `the day`
            THEN `a significant political affiliation (and no disqualifying one)`
        OTHERWISE `neither`

§§§ `s 6 — Definitions`

-- designated diplomatic office            -> s 7 above
-- disqualifying political affiliation     -> s 8(1) above
-- significant political affiliation       -> s 8(2) above
-- Selection Committee                     -> s 12(2), selection-process.l4
-- rules                                   -> s 16, miscellaneous.l4
-- Minister: the Minister administering the Diplomatic and Consular Missions
--   Act 1978. Every duty and power below is the Minister's in this sense.
-- Secretary: defined and never used: ISSUE 19.
DECLARE `Actor` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the Selection Committee`
    `the person who makes the appointment or arrangement`

§§ `Part 1 — illustrations`

`a person with no political history` MEANS `Person` WITH
    `name`                                              IS "Avery"
    `periods of membership of a legislature`            IS EMPTY
    `engagements under the MOP(S) Act`                  IS EMPTY
    `engagements as State or Territory political staff` IS EMPTY
    `roles with political parties`                      IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` `Ambassador to Japan`
#ASSERT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`Consul-General in the United States of America` "Chicago")
#ASSERT NOT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`another office of the Commonwealth` "Ambassador to France" TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `a person with no political history` `on` (`the date` 2028 6 1) EQUALS `neither`
#ASSERT (`s 2 — the day this Act commences, given` (`the date` 2026 12 31)) `is the same day as` (`the date` 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT (`s 2 — the day this Act commences, given` (`the date` 2027 2 28)) `is the same day as` (`the date` 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT (`s 2 — the day this Act commences, given` (`the date` 2027 6 10)) `is the same day as` (`the date` 2027 6 11)
